As a consensual role-script, yes: status is reciprocal.

If one person wants to be treated like a queen while treating the other like a disposable servant, the game collapses. “King” and “queen” only work as paired roles because each confers dignity, responsibility, loyalty, protection, admiration, and obligation on the other.

So the healthier structure is not:

submit because one sex is inherently above the other.

It is:

choose the polarity → honor the role → receive the reciprocal role.

In that frame, submission is not worthlessness; it is voluntary trust. Dominance is not license; it is accepted responsibility. And either person can refuse, renegotiate, or leave the role.

That’s why the archetype works when it works: the crown is granted, not seized.